! ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
! Parker Physics — SWMF coupled GM + IE run, driven by L1 IMF
! ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
! Components:
!   GM (Geo-magnetosphere)    BATS-R-US around Earth
!   IE (Ionosphere)            Ridley_serial (RIM)
!
! Coupling:
!   L1 IMF.dat → GM upstream BC (#UPSTREAM_INPUT_FILE)
!   GM ↔ IE every DtCouple seconds in the time-accurate phase
!
! Outputs:
!   GM_log_*.log  RAW, 60s cadence — Bz, Pdyn, etc. at Earth subsolar BC
!   IE_log_*.dat  60s cadence — CPCP_n, CPCP_s, HP_n, HP_s
!                 → parse_ie_log.py extracts Φ_PC = max(N,S), HPI = N+S
!
! Generated by gen_param.py — do not edit directly.
! Authoritative template at: swmf/config/PARAM.in.GM_IE
!
! COLD-START LADDER (do not collapse into a single session):
! A cold magnetosphere cannot be integrated directly in 2nd-order, time-
! accurate mode — the discontinuous initial state overshoots into negative
! density/pressure on iteration 1 ("negative fast speed squared"). The
! validated SWPC Geospace _init recipe relaxes first:
!   Session 1  #TIMEACCURATE F, #SCHEME 1 (1st order)  — relax 700 iters
!   Session 2  #TIMEACCURATE F, #SCHEME 2 mc3          — converge 1500 iters
!   Session 3  #TIMEACCURATE T, #BORIS + #MINIMUMPRESSURE — drive the storm
! Structure mirrors SWMFsoftware/SWMF Param/SWPC/PARAM.in_SWPC_simple_init,
! adapted to GM+IE only (no IM/RB) and to our Rusanov flux.
! ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

#DESCRIPTION
Parker Physics Phase-0 hindcast: GM + IE driven by L1 IMF		StringDescription

! Processor layout. Current SWMF reads the component map from PARAM.in (the
! standalone LAYOUT.in is legacy and is NOT consulted) — without this block
! setup_from_file aborts with "could not find #LAYOUT or #COMPONENTMAP".
! GM gets ranks 0..N-2, IE (serial) gets the last rank. For -n 4: GM 0-2, IE 3.
#COMPONENTMAP
GM			0  -2  1
IE			-1 -1  1

! Session 1 begins in STEADY-STATE (local time stepping). Time only advances
! once session 3 flips this to T — so ${STOP_TIME_S} below is wall-clock storm
! duration measured from #STARTTIME, unaffected by the relaxation iterations.
#TIMEACCURATE
F			IsTimeAccurate

! Simulation start time — filled in per-run by gen_param.py
#STARTTIME
${YEAR}			iYear
${MONTH}		iMonth
${DAY}			iDay
${HOUR}			iHour
${MINUTE}		iMinute
0			iSecond
0.0			FracSecond

#COMPONENT
GM			NameComp
T			UseComp

#COMPONENT
IE			NameComp
T			UseComp

! ── GM↔IE coupling (steady-state phase) ──────────────────────────────────────
! Couple every 10 iterations while relaxing; switched to a 5 s time cadence in
! the time-accurate session 3. GM passes field-aligned currents to IE; IE
! passes the potential back to GM.
#COUPLE2
GM			NameComp1
IE			NameComp2
10			DnCouple
-1.0			DtCouple


! ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
!  BEGIN_COMP GM ─ Geo-magnetosphere (BATS-R-US)
! ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#BEGIN_COMP GM ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

! GSM frame — Sun-Earth line + Earth's rotation axis projection
#COORDINATESYSTEM
GSM			TypeCoordSystem

! GM grid: ±32 R_E sunward, -224 R_E tail, ±64 R_E flank.
! Standard Phase-0 box; gives ~6 R_E resolution in the inner mag.
#GRID
2			nRootBlock1  (X)
1			nRootBlock2  (Y)
1			nRootBlock3  (Z)
-224.0			xMin [R_E]   (tail)
  32.0			xMax [R_E]   (sunward)
 -64.0			yMin [R_E]
  64.0			yMax [R_E]
 -64.0			zMin [R_E]
  64.0			zMax [R_E]

! Grid resolution targets — refine inner mag, coarsen tail.
#GRIDRESOLUTION
1.0			AreaResolution
initial			NameArea

#GRIDRESOLUTION
0.25			AreaResolution
sphere0			NameArea
6.0			Radius

#GRIDRESOLUTION
0.5			AreaResolution
sphere0
12.0			Radius

! Inner body (Earth) and field-aligned-current mapping radius.
! rCurrents is the radius at which GM extracts FACs to map down to IE along
! dipole field lines. It MUST exceed rBody and the planet radius, or the
! GM↔IE coupling aborts in map_planet_field with "mapping radius is less than
! planet radius" (rMap=0.0). Values from the validated reference
! SWMFsoftware/BATSRUS Param/EARTH/PARAM.in — do not zero these out.
#BODY
T			UseBody
2.5			rBody      [rEarth]
3.5			rCurrents  [rEarth]
28.0			BodyRhoDim [amu/cc]
25000.0			BodyTDim   [K]

! Inner boundary (Earth ionosphere shell).
#INNERBOUNDARY
ionosphere		TypeBcInner

! Raise the inner-boundary density with the cross-polar-cap potential so the
! near-Earth plasma does not collapse to negative density during the storm.
! Uses CPCP from the coupled IE solution. From the SWPC Geospace recipe.
#CPCPBOUNDARY
T			UseCpcpBc
28.0			Rho0Cpcp   [amu/cc]
0.1			RhoPerCpcp [amu/cc per kV]

! Outer boundaries: outflow on tail and flanks; upstream face driven by IMF.
#OUTERBOUNDARY
outflow			TypeBc1   (-x, tail)
vary			TypeBc2   (+x, sunward face — driven by #UPSTREAM_INPUT_FILE)
outflow			TypeBc3   (-y)
outflow			TypeBc4   (+y)
outflow			TypeBc5   (-z)
outflow			TypeBc6   (+z)

! Drive the +x boundary with L1 IMF, time-shifted to bow shock nose by OMNI.
! ${IMF_FILE} is filled by gen_param.py and points at the file written by
! swmf/pipeline/fetch_omni_imf.py. Read once at start; held fixed during the
! steady-state relaxation, then advanced through the storm in session 3.
#UPSTREAM_INPUT_FILE
T			UseUpstreamInputFile
${IMF_FILE}		NameUpstreamFile
0.0			SatelliteYPos [R_E]   (project Y → 0 since OMNI does too)
0.0			SatelliteZPos [R_E]

! Session 1 scheme: 1st-order Rusanov — most diffusive, relaxes the cold
! initial condition without producing negative states. Upgraded in session 2.
#SCHEME
1			nOrder
Rusanov			TypeFlux

! Boris semi-relativistic correction — ON FOR THE ENTIRE RUN, set here in
! session 1 and persisted (SWMF carries parameters forward across #RUN
! boundaries until overridden). Boris caps the artificial fast/Alfvén speed
! where B is huge and rho is low (near Earth), which otherwise forces a
! vanishing time step or a blow-up.
!
! CRITICAL — load-bearing placement: Boris MUST be active during the
! steady-state relaxation, not switched on only at the time-accurate session.
! Boris redefines the conserved momentum (it folds in the v×B electric-field
! term). A previous revision enabled #BORIS only in session 3; the relaxed
! state then carried the NON-Boris momentum definition, so the first
! time-accurate step detonated the inner-boundary cell at r~3.5 R_E
! (NaN from advance_explicit, density → 1e100), independent of nStage/CFL.
! Relaxing WITH Boris on keeps the conserved state consistent across the
! transition. Factor 0.02 follows the validated SWPC Geospace recipe.
#BORIS
T			UseBorisCorrection
0.02			BorisClightFactor

! Positivity floor, also active for the whole run — BATSRUS clips pressure
! here instead of crashing on a storm-time negative-pressure transient.
#MINIMUMPRESSURE
1e-5			pMinDim [nPa]

! Non-conservative pressure update inside 6 R_E (standard for storm-time
! magnetosphere stability), conservative beyond. From the validated reference
! SWMFsoftware/BATSRUS Param/EARTH/PARAM.in.
#NONCONSERVATIVE
T			UseNonConservative

#CONSERVATIVECRITERIA
1			nConservCrit
r			TypeConservCrit
6.0			rConserv

! Log file: 60s cadence for solar-wind / magnetopause monitoring at the
! subsolar point — plug source for Bz, Pdyn timeseries downstream.
#SAVELOGFILE
T			DoSaveLogfile
RAW step time		StringLog
-1			DnSaveLogfile
60.0			DtSaveLogfile [seconds]

#END_COMP GM ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


! ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
!  BEGIN_COMP IE ─ Ionosphere (Ridley_serial / RIM)
! ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#BEGIN_COMP IE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

! Ionospheric conductance model. CONDUCTANCE empirical (F10.7-driven solar
! EUV + auroral precipitation from GM) is the Phase-0 default. Higher-fidelity
! models (e.g. RIDLEY_SERIAL_AUR) are Phase-2 territory.
#IONOSPHERE
5			TypeConductanceModel  (5 = empirical EUV + auroral)
T			UseFullCurrent
T			UseFakeRegion2
${F107_SFU}		F107Flux
1.0			StarLightPedConductance
0.25			PolarCapPedConductance

! Save the IE log file every 60 s. parse_ie_log.py reads CPCP_n, CPCP_s,
! HP_n, HP_s from this.
#SAVELOGFILE
T			DoSaveLogfile
60.0			DtSaveLogfile [seconds]

! Snapshot the full ionospheric pattern every 5 min (for visualisation).
#SAVEPLOT
1			nPlotFile
min idl			StringPlot
-1			DnSavePlot
300.0			DtSavePlot [seconds]

#END_COMP IE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

! End of session 1 — relax the cold start in 1st order, steady state.
#STOP
700			MaxIteration
-1.0			tSimulationMax


! ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
!  SESSION 2 — still steady-state, upgrade to 2nd order to converge the
!  magnetosphere shape before driving it. (#RUN ends the previous session.)
! ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#RUN ###########################################################################

#BEGIN_COMP GM ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

! 2nd-order Rusanov + sharp mc3 limiter, 2-stage explicit at a conservative CFL.
#SCHEME
2			nOrder
Rusanov			TypeFlux
mc3			TypeLimiter
1.2			LimiterBeta

#TIMESTEPPING
2			nStage
0.6			CflExpl

#END_COMP GM ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

#STOP
1500			MaxIteration
-1.0			tSimulationMax


! ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
!  SESSION 3 — time-accurate production phase. Drive the storm from the relaxed
!  steady state. The Boris correction and minimum-pressure floor are ALREADY
!  active here — they were set in session 1 and persist across #RUN. Do NOT
!  re-enable Boris only at this session: see the CRITICAL note on #BORIS above.
! ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#RUN ###########################################################################

#TIMEACCURATE
T			IsTimeAccurate

! Switch GM↔IE coupling to a 5 s time cadence for the time-accurate phase.
#COUPLE2
GM			NameComp1
IE			NameComp2
-1			DnCouple
5.0			DtCouple

#PROGRESS
100			DnProgressShort
1000			DnProgressLong

! Save state every 1 simulated hour for crash recovery over the long run.
#SAVERESTART
T			DoSaveRestart
-1			DnSaveRestart
3600.0			DtSaveRestart

#BEGIN_COMP GM ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

! Boris correction and #MINIMUMPRESSURE are inherited from session 1 (SWMF
! persists parameters across #RUN) — intentionally NOT repeated here so the
! relaxed steady state and this time-accurate phase share one consistent,
! Boris-aware conserved state. See the CRITICAL #BORIS note in session 1.
!
! 2-stage Runge-Kutta at a conservative CFL. The SWPC reference also offers a
! 1-stage + CflExpl 0.85 variant; with Boris consistent across the transition
! either is stable, and RK2/0.6 is the more robust 2nd-order choice here.
#TIMESTEPPING
2			nStage
0.6			CflExpl

#END_COMP GM ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

! Total storm duration. gen_param.py sets ${STOP_TIME_S}; time advances only
! in this session, so this is the simulated wall-clock span from #STARTTIME.
#STOP
-1			MaxIteration
${STOP_TIME_S}		tSimulationMax

#END
